<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#pepper">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pepper</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pepper is a spice made from the dried berries of a vine native to southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, long one of the most valuable goods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade">Indian Ocean trade</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>'s control of the sea route to India allowed it to profit enormously from the pepper trade in the early sixteenth century. A West African pepper was also among the goods exported from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a> to Portuguese traders.</p></div>
